[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span> has a developed new way to discover lemmas <code>#click_suggestions</code>, the first version is merged into Mathlib. However, in the following example, when clicking on the whole goal, it doesn't find the lemma I expect (<code>exact?</code> finds it, and it is reducibly applicable). Do you know what is going on, Jovan?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">click_suggestions</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">measurePreserving_updateFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">updateFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- with_reducible exact measurable_updateFinset</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 605957884,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1782208448
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the report! We can inspect the problem using <code>set_option click_suggestions.debug true</code>, which shows that the lemma is found (so it is not a discrimination tree issue), but fails with this unhelpful error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">measurable_updateFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">updateFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">updateFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It turns out that this unification only works with <code>foApprox := true</code> in the configuration. This holds by default when running tactics, but for some reason the default value of <code>foApprox</code> is <code>false</code>. I've created a fix in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40956\">#40956</a>.</p>",
        "id": 606017441,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1782224483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>#click_suggestions</code> is already very nice!<br>\nI found another click_suggestions error. The following example panics if you click on the <code>False</code> in the hypothesis <code>h</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ClickSuggestions</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">click_suggestions</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lmarginal_lmarginal_compl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606231763,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1782305086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! The issue is related to the fact that the <code>False</code> is actually an uninstantiated metavariable. I've fixed it in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41001\">#41001</a></p>",
        "id": 606246849,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1782308647
    }
]